==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Wind Dancer Valkyrie''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit is mostly used as a generalist or as a quick, high DPS unit. She has added abilities that make her better against [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]], [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|wave attackers]], status-inflicting enemies and [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]]. She acts almost as though she were [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] but with with less DPS and speed, in exchange for more range and a faster recharge, which means she can be stacked in stages where she isn't outranged.

Her high damage and DPS, medium range and high speed make her a great suicide bomber to deal insane damage and then die, similar to [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Yukimura]]. However, she gets hit easily because of her movement speed. Lengthy foreswing (1.06 seconds) can also be a problem.

She is best on stages where she can get inside the enemies' blind spot, so she can take advantage of her Zombie Killer/high DPS/wave immunity. Note that this unit has a hard time surviving for long, due to low health, range and knockbacks, but also because of her excessive speed and immunity to abilities that would let her reposition, being Knockback and Warp.

